  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Aces and Kings. Logic: Complete all eight foundations, four building up from ace to king and four building down from king to ace, without regard to suit.',
    Player: 'Aces and Kings is a difficult two-deck solitaire in which eight foundations build both upward from aces and downward from kings without regard to suit.',
    objective: 'Build the four ace foundations up to kings by color while managing the corner waste piles.',
    gameplay: 'Remove the aces to form the central foundations, then deal through the remaining stock. Cards may be built to foundations by color sequence, while waste piles at the corners hold cards that cannot yet be used.',
    keyRules: [
      'Four aces start the foundations.',
      'Foundations build upward by color rather than exact suit.',
      'Corner waste piles create the distinctive layout and restrict later access.',
    ],
